  "cross_component_finding": {
    "observation": "This fts/ page names two RBAC roles, 'FTS Admin' and 'FTS Searcher', for creating indexes and performing searches respectively. The newer search/ tree's create-quick-index.md instead names a single 'Search Admin' role for creating a Search index. These are very likely either (a) the same underlying RBAC roles referred to by an old vs. new product name ('FTS' vs 'Search'), or (b) distinct roles where the newer docs have dropped the searcher-side role from view. Either way this is a terminology/reconciliation flag between the two component trees for the coordinator - I minted separate privilege concepts (privilege:fts-admin, privilege:fts-searcher, privilege:search-admin) rather than guessing an equivalence, since no page states the mapping explicitly.",
    "docsIssue": null
  },
